# TSan suppression for the pre-existing, benign data race in slab_pool_alloc
# when called concurrently from multiple stepcompress producer threads sharing
# the global qm_pool (defined in msgblock.c).
#
# What: the carve-fresh-chunk slow path of slab_pool_alloc writes to
# slab_pool->chunks without synchronization.  slab_pool.h documents this
# explicitly: "the carve-fresh-chunk path writes to ->chunks without
# synchronization; allocations from a single owner are the supported model."
#
# Why benign: qm_pool is process-lifetime; the chunks list only grows and is
# never read back by concurrent allocators.  The worst outcome of a lost write
# is a bounded chunk leak — queue_message objects themselves are allocated
# correctly via the CAS fast path.
#
# Scope: suppresses only races whose call stack contains slab_pool_alloc.
# Any race introduced by the twin-stepper handoff primitive (which uses
# separate synchronization paths) will still be reported by TSan.
race:slab_pool_alloc
